Fastokens is officially merged into SGLang. This is an open-source Rust BPE tokenizer from @CrusoeAI, built with @nvidia Dynamo, which offers up to 50% faster TTFT on agentic workloads using real production traffic and over 10x average speedup compared to HuggingFace tokenizers.

It works across models like DeepSeek, Qwen, Kimi, MiniMax, and Nemotron. Huge thanks to the @CrusoeAI team for the collaboration.

@CrusoeAI: "Most teams scale inference by adding more GPUs. Smart teams think about how tokens flow. Introducing fastokens — Crusoe's open-source Rust tokenizer, built with NVIDIA Dynamo, now merged into SGLang. Up to 50% faster TTFT for agentic workloads, measured on real production traffic!"

Meet MiniCPM-V 4.6 from @OpenBMB, a 1.3B edge-friendly multimodal LLM with superior efficiency. Day-0 support is now live in SGLang!

Leading capabilities include a score of 13 on the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index benchmark and strong multimodal performance, matching Qwen3.5 2B-level capacity across five major visual language benchmarks. It is ultra-efficient, requiring over 50% less visual FLOPs via LLaVA-UHD v4 and mixed 4x/16x visual token compression, and is mobile-ready for deployment across iOS, Android, and HarmonyOS.

@OpenBMB: "MiniCPM-V 4.6 (1.3B) is now live. High-res visual processing is optimized for consumer-grade and mobile hardware. We’ve leveraged the latest LLaVA-UHD v4 technique to cut vision encoding costs by 55%, enabling native edge deployment with extreme efficiency. It beats Gemma4-E2B-it and Qwen3.5-0.8B across key multimodal and Artificial Analysis benchmarks, scoring higher than Qwen3.5-0.8B using just 2.5% of its token budget. It is 2.2x faster than Qwen3.5-0.8B, even with 3136² high-res images, and has ~1.5x token throughput compared to Qwen3.5-0.8B on a single RTX 4090."

Thinky's secret plan involves increasing human-AI bandwidth, raising the ceiling of human+AI intelligence, and helping humans remain the main characters in the new world. We are currently at Step 1, where Interaction Models serve as effective real-time collaborative tools for humans.

@thinkymachines: "People talk, listen, watch, think, and collaborate at the same time, in real time. We've designed an AI that works with people the same way. We share our approach, early results, and a quick look at our model in action."

Interaction models move beyond turn-based AI interfaces by handling multimodal, real-time collaboration natively across audio, video, and text.

Sharing our work on full-duplex multimodal models that enable real-time interaction that's natural and intuitive without compromising on intelligence. We started Thinky to differentially advance capabilities for human-AI collaboration, which are often underemphasized compared to intelligence and autonomy because they are harder to evaluate.

In the future, we envision that every AI system will incorporate an interaction model as the outer user-facing layer, continually keeping the user informed and learning what they actually want.

