Loved this one. Drafters lose their attention sink as hidden-state magnitudes grow with each speculation step. Moving RMSNorm allows the drafter to learn to be a depth-independent predictor instead of using stacked verifier layers.

The result is a 2× acceptance under perturbation, 1.18× longer context, and a 30% lower training cost. GPT-OSS speculative decoding models achieve up to 50% throughput on long context and large batches and are ready for day-0 deployment on SGLang.

@dogacel0: "As a part of our research, we are releasing the fastest GPT-OSS speculative decoding models out there, increasing throughput up to 50% on long context and large batches! Available on day-0 with SGLang! Huge thanks to @sgl_project and @lmsysorg."
